| SeekEnd: each clip decoded to the end, then vcdec_flush (after the
| end of the stream the decoder is created again) and on from the last
| keyframe to the end again: a seek after the end, which lost the last
| two pictures with a flush alone. The small and hd clips. Reports to
| ResultEnd.
| (a GCCSDK program: needs SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport loaded)
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error This needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error This needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
WimpSlot -min 16384K -max 16384K
Remove <Obey$Dir>.ResultEnd
Run <Obey$Dir>.vcdectest -n -E -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultEnd <Obey$Dir>.clips.small.mp4 <Obey$Dir>.clips.small.crc <Obey$Dir>.clips.small.sig
Run <Obey$Dir>.vcdectest -n -E -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultEnd <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.mp4 <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.crc <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.sig
